<p>In 2015, Canadian politician Sheldon Bergson changed his name to Above Znoneofthe, so that it would appear on electoral ballots as &#8220;Znoneofthe, Above.&#8221; (The Z, which is silent, ensures that the name will appear last in a list of candidates.)</p>
<p>He ran in an Ontario provincial by-election the following year, winning 0.43 percent of the vote, and has participated in several races since. Amazingly, <a href="https://www.futilitycloset.com/2011/09/24/civic-minded-2/">he&#8217;s not the first person to try this</a>.</p>
<p>(Thanks, Alessia.)</p>
